IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for two forks of the time module registered in pass 2.  F3: the second reading of s 61(1)(c) with s 61(1)(e), the
-- function that rolls BACK from an excluded last day, beside the function that rolls FORWARD (the reading taken).  F13: a day
-- specified for subsidiary legislation that is before its publication.  Expected values are written from the sections and from
-- hand calendar arithmetic: 1 Feb 2024 is a Thursday, so Fri 9 Feb, Sat 10 Feb, Sun 11 Feb, Mon 12 Feb 2024, and Thu 8 Feb 2024;
-- 1 Mar 2025 is a Saturday, so Fri 7 Mar, Sat 8 Mar, Sun 9 Mar, Mon 10 Mar 2025, Tue 11 Mar, Wed 12 Mar 2025.

§ `Tests -- the other reading of a time before a day`

GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`no holidays` MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`            IS EMPTY
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS EMPTY
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS EMPTY

GIVEN a IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`public holidays on` a MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`            IS EMPTY
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS EMPTY
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS a

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      named IS A DATE
      h IS A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`test rolling forward, the reading taken` n named h MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time within a time before a day` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS n, `unit` IS `in days`) named h
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `end`'s `last day for doing the thing`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      named IS A DATE
      h IS A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`test rolling back, the other reading` n named h MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time within a time before a day, rolling back from an excluded last day, the other reading` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS n, `unit` IS `in days`) named h
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `end`'s `last day for doing the thing`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      named IS A DATE
      h IS A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`test rolling back, the last day by the calendar` n named h MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time within a time before a day, rolling back from an excluded last day, the other reading` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS n, `unit` IS `in days`) named h
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `end`'s `last day by the calendar`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      named IS A DATE
      h IS A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`test rolling back, the first day` n named h MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time within a time before a day, rolling back from an excluded last day, the other reading` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS n, `unit` IS `in days`) named h
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `first day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `10 days before Sunday 11 February 2024: the last day by the calendar is Saturday 10 February`

-- s 61(1)(c): the time does not include the named day, so the 10 days are 1 to 10 February; the last day by the calendar is a Saturday.
#ASSERT `test rolling back, the first day` 10 (Date 11 2 2024) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2024)
#ASSERT `test rolling back, the last day by the calendar` 10 (Date 11 2 2024) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 2 2024)
-- s 61(1)(e) as written (the reading taken): the thing may be done on the next day that is not an excluded day, Monday 12 February,
-- which is AFTER the named day.
#ASSERT `test rolling forward, the reading taken` 10 (Date 11 2 2024) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 12 2 2024)
-- the other reading: the thing must be done by Friday 9 February.
#ASSERT `test rolling back, the other reading` 10 (Date 11 2 2024) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 9 2 2024)

§§ `With a public holiday on the Friday as well`

#ASSERT `test rolling forward, the reading taken` 10 (Date 11 2 2024) (`public holidays on` (LIST Date 9 2 2024)) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 2 2024)
#ASSERT `test rolling back, the other reading` 10 (Date 11 2 2024) (`public holidays on` (LIST Date 9 2 2024)) EQUALS JUST (Date 8 2 2024)

§§ `7 days before Monday 10 March 2025 (the F3 example): the last day by the calendar is Sunday 9 March`

#ASSERT `test rolling forward, the reading taken` 7 (Date 10 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
#ASSERT `test rolling back, the other reading` 7 (Date 10 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 7 3 2025)

§§ `The two readings agree when the last day by the calendar is not an excluded day`

-- 7 days before Wednesday 12 March 2025: 5 to 11 March, last day Tuesday 11 March.
#ASSERT `test rolling forward, the reading taken` 7 (Date 12 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2025)
#ASSERT `test rolling back, the other reading` 7 (Date 12 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2025)

§§ `Only a whole number of days of at least 1 can be counted back from a day`

#ASSERT `the time within a time before a day, rolling back from an excluded last day, the other reading` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit` IS `in months`) (Date 10 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the time within a time before a day, rolling back from an excluded last day, the other reading` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS 0, `unit` IS `in days`) (Date 10 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the time within a time before a day, rolling back from an excluded last day, the other reading` (`Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS 1.5, `unit` IS `in days`) (Date 10 3 2025) `no holidays` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- subsidiary legislation naming a day before it is published (fork F13)`

-- s 41(1)(b) places no limit on the specified day; the day is returned whatever it is.  For an Act, s 23(a) does bar a day
-- before the proclamation is published, and that bar is a separate function.
#ASSERT `the day subsidiary legislation comes into operation` (Date 5 3 2025) (JUST (Date 1 3 2025)) EQUALS (Date 1 3 2025)
#ASSERT `the day subsidiary legislation comes into operation` (Date 5 3 2025) (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) EQUALS (Date 5 3 2025)
#ASSERT `the power to fix a day extends to a day not prior to publication` (Date 5 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the power to fix a day extends to a day not prior to publication` (Date 5 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
